bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    seed_native_build_interpreted_startup_spin_2026-11-09, P1, open, "Seed native-build (2026-11-05 seed, aarch64) spins >=45 min at 99% single-CPU with zero output on a cold cache; spin is backend-independent (llvm==cranelift), entry-independent (hello_native==3-line trivial entry), and sits in the seed-INTERPRETed Simple driver startup after module loading (compile-source-inventory / parse-closure publication walk), before any codegen; original 2.7s cranelift contrast not reproducible under identical flags", src/compiler_rust, 0, doc/08_tracking/bug/seed_native_build_interpreted_startup_spin_2026-11-09.md, 2026-11-09, 2026-11-09, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_native_build_interpreted_startup_spin_2026-11-09, 1, "2026-11-09 diagnosis lane (worktree build/agent-worktrees/boot-llvmdiagnose @ origin/release/1.0.0 bbe3d42f0e0, seed sha256 df9dfb057afb7b8f... aarch64 20-core). Repro command shape: seed native-build --backend <llvm|cranelift> [--entry-closure] --threads 8 --runtime-bundle auto --cache-dir <private> --entry examples/01_getting_started/hello_native.spl -o <out>."
    seed_native_build_interpreted_startup_spin_2026-11-09, 2, "Discriminator results (all cold private caches, run in parallel): (1) llvm lane: 10-min timeout kill, 99% CPU 1 core, RSS 1.65-1.73GB flat then GC dip to 1.30GB, build log frozen at 107157 bytes, ZERO cache objects, ZERO output; (2) cranelift lane with IDENTICAL flags: same behavior, still spinning at >=5 min (previous session's 2.7s cranelift claim NOT reproducible; no examples/hello_world.spl exists in-tree); (3) cranelift WITHOUT --entry-closure: identical spin; (4) 3-line trivial entry (no imports): identical spin, killed by 240s timeout, log frozen at the same 107157 bytes, no output."
    seed_native_build_interpreted_startup_spin_2026-11-09, 3, "Where the spin is: RUST_LOG=info trace (spans) shows the seed runs run_file_with_args{path=src/app/cli/native_build_main.spl} -- the native-build driver is INTERPRETED Simple, not Rust. Phase timeline: ~1 min of load_and_merge_module (852 modules, compiler driver+backend+linker sources) with log growth 53KB->1.1MB, then total silence. Last spans before freeze: native_build_parse_closure_owner -> linker_wrapper/elf_writer module loads, then check-dbs workaround note; after that zero trace output even at debug level for >=10 min. /proc/<pid>/io rchar flat (252484115 -> 252484115 over 30s) during spin: pure in-memory compute, no file reads. Only 1 running thread of 5; workers idle; not a deadlock (CPU pegged)."
    seed_native_build_interpreted_startup_spin_2026-11-09, 4, "Root-cause classification: NOT (a) LLVM codegen slow -- no codegen ever starts (zero cache objects, phase is pre-backend); NOT (b) an llvm-lane-specific cache/exe-identity defect (hir_cache class) -- backend- AND entry-independent, and the failure precedes cache-key computation; NOT (c) thread starvation/deadlock -- single hot thread, 95-99% user CPU. It is a backend-independent pathological startup cost in the seed-executed interpreted driver, suspected the full-checkout compile-source-inventory build / parse-closure publication walk (src/lib/scv/compile_source_inventory_core.spl itself notes 'cold inventory that was ~200 s of the ~360 s Stage 2 cold init (x86_64)'; interpreted aarch64 seed plausibly 50-100x that). Finite-vs-infinite unproven: no completion or phase transition observed in >=45 min (original lane) or 10 min (repro); RSS GC cycling hints at progress but no marker exists."
    seed_native_build_interpreted_startup_spin_2026-11-09, 5, "The 2026-11-09 boot-llvm lane contrast (llvm 45 min vs cranelift 2.7s) is an artifact: the cranelift lane's worktree/evidence is gone, no warm cache exists at the default location (.simple/native_cache empty; seed writes cache only at completion), and under identical flags both backends spin identically. Likely the 2.7s run consumed a pre-populated private cache from an earlier completed run in that lane (cache-hit path skips the spin) or measured a different invocation. Follow-ups: (1) run seed native-build cold under gdb/perf on a ptrace-permitted host to name the exact hot fn; (2) check whether the inventory/closure walk is quadratic in checkout file count (worktree has 145004 files); (3) add a periodic progress/log heartbeat to the interpreted driver's post-load startup phases so future freezes are attributable."

